    "boil": 0.25
  },
  "sources": [
    "Uri Gneezy, Ernan Haruvy and Hadas Yafe, \"The Inefficiency of Splitting the Bill\", The Economic Journal, vol. 114, no. 495, April 2004, pages 265 to 280. A field experiment in a restaurant: diners who split the bill equally ate more than diners who each paid for their own, and they said they preferred paying for their own. https://ideas.repec.org/a/ecj/econjl/v114y2004i495p265-280.html",
    "What the story invents: the four friends, the restaurant and the prices. Three lobsters at $60 is $180, split four ways $45 each, the glass of water included."
